    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d377">

                <pb facs="0381" n="371" sameAs="frus:frus1943v01/pg371"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">840.48 Refugees/4711: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-10-28T16:00:00+01:00">October 28, 1943—4
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received October 28—4 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>7452. Pursuant to Embassy’s 7341, October 25, 4 p.m.,<anchor n="45"
                        xml:id="d377-f1"/> we have now received from the Foreign Office a letter
                    dated October 26 which states as follows: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“We concur in the point of view put forward by the State Department and
                            have asked Mr. Macmillan to give Mr. Murphy any support which may be
                            necessary to ensure that the French conditions should be interpreted as
                            liberally as possible. We added that in particular it seemed desirable
                            that all suitable refugees should be allowed to take up some form of
                            employment.</p>
                        <p>I understand from you that the French authorities have now consented to
                            review the position, and I shall be interested to hear the result, so
                            that the exodus from Spain can begin without any further delay.”</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Winant</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
